#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"id2\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mode-based indexing {#mode-based-indexing}"
msgstr "Pengindeksan berbasis mode {#mode-based-indexing}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "All operator representations refer to the indices that their terms act upon as **modes**. A mode is simply an index identifying a fermionic degree of freedom in your system. The mapping from physical degrees of freedom (such as spatial orbitals, spin states, or other quantum numbers) to mode indices is left to the user, enabling maximum flexibility.\n"
msgstr "Semua representasi operator menyebut indeks yang menjadi sasaran term-nya sebagai **mode**. Mode itu cuma sebuah indeks yang mengidentifikasi satu derajat kebebasan fermionik di sistem kamu. Pemetaan dari derajat kebebasan fisik (seperti orbital spasial, keadaan spin, atau bilangan kuantum lainnya) ke indeks mode diserahkan ke pengguna, jadi fleksibilitasnya maksimal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This abstraction is also present in the [`qiskit_fermions.circuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit#module-qiskit_fermions.circuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit\") module, where the [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") operates on a register of fermionic modes. In both the operator and circuit representations, modes provide a consistent, algebra-independent way to specify which degrees of freedom participate in a given operation.\n"
msgstr "Abstraksi ini juga ada di modul [`qiskit_fermions.circuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit#module-qiskit_fermions.circuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit\"), tempat [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") beroperasi pada sebuah register mode fermionik. Baik di representasi operator maupun circuit, mode menyediakan cara yang konsisten dan tidak bergantung pada aljabar untuk menentukan derajat kebebasan mana yang terlibat dalam suatu operasi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Important\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  **Current implementations use spinless modes**: All operator representations currently provided by this module treat modes as spinless fermionic degrees of freedom. This means if your system has both spin-up and spin-down electrons or fermions, you must explicitly map them to distinct modes (for example, modes 0-3 for spin-up of four spatial orbitals, modes 4-7 for spin-down, or any other convention you choose).\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Penting\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  **Implementasi saat ini memakai mode tanpa spin**: Semua representasi operator yang saat ini disediakan modul ini memperlakukan mode sebagai derajat kebebasan fermionik tanpa spin. Artinya, kalau sistem kamu punya elektron atau fermion dengan spin-up dan spin-down, kamu harus memetakannya secara eksplisit ke mode yang berbeda (misalnya mode 0-3 untuk spin-up dari empat orbital spasial, mode 4-7 untuk spin-down, atau konvensi lain yang kamu pilih).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  This design keeps the core representations simple and general while avoiding imposing a specific spin-ordering convention. Utility modules like [`qiskit_fermions.operators.library`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-library#module-qiskit_fermions.operators.library \"qiskit_fermions.operators.library\") provide convenience functions (for example, [`FCIDump.from_file()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-library-fci-dump#qiskit_fermions.operators.library.FCIDump.from_file \"qiskit_fermions.operators.library.FCIDump.from_file\")) that handle such mappings for you when loading electronic structure data.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Desain ini menjaga representasi inti tetap sederhana dan umum, sekaligus menghindari pemaksaan konvensi urutan spin tertentu. Modul utilitas seperti [`qiskit_fermions.operators.library`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-library#module-qiskit_fermions.operators.library \"qiskit_fermions.operators.library\") menyediakan fungsi praktis (misalnya [`FCIDump.from_file()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-library-fci-dump#qiskit_fermions.operators.library.FCIDump.from_file \"qiskit_fermions.operators.library.FCIDump.from_file\")) yang menangani pemetaan semacam itu buat kamu saat memuat data struktur elektronik.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Hint\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  As the package evolves, spinful operator representations might be added that natively support spin degrees of freedom in their data model. These will be clearly distinguished from the current spinless implementations and will coexist with them in the module.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Petunjuk\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Seiring berkembangnya paket ini, representasi operator dengan spin mungkin akan ditambahkan, yang mendukung derajat kebebasan spin secara native di model datanya. Representasi itu akan dibedakan dengan jelas dari implementasi tanpa spin yang ada sekarang dan akan hidup berdampingan dengannya di modul ini.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"term-grouping\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Term grouping and commutation relationships {#term-grouping-and-commutation-relationships}"
msgstr "Pengelompokan term dan relasi komutasi {#term-grouping-and-commutation-relationships}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Like the coefficients and mode indices, operators can optionally store a **groups array** that associates each term with a group index. By integrating grouping directly into the operator representation as part of the sparse data structure, grouping information naturally travels with the operator through transformations. This enables systematic structure usage, whether from physical properties, algebraic relationships, or problem-specific symmetries. The structured information can then be used in downstream operations like circuit synthesis and decomposition by using methods like [`OperatorTrait.split_out_groups()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.split_out_groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.split_out_groups\").\n"
msgstr "Seperti koefisien dan indeks mode, operator bisa menyimpan **array groups** secara opsional yang mengaitkan setiap term dengan sebuah indeks grup. Dengan memasukkan pengelompokan langsung ke representasi operator sebagai bagian dari struktur data sparse, informasi pengelompokan otomatis ikut terbawa bersama operator lewat berbagai transformasi. Ini memungkinkan pemakaian struktur secara sistematis, entah berasal dari properti fisik, relasi aljabar, atau simetri khusus masalah. Informasi terstruktur itu lalu bisa dipakai di operasi lanjutan seperti sintesis dan dekomposisi circuit dengan metode seperti [`OperatorTrait.split_out_groups()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.split_out_groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.split_out_groups\").\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For detailed guidance on how to group operator terms in your workflows, see the [grouping](grouping#grouping-explanation) guide.\n"
msgstr "Untuk panduan lengkap soal cara mengelompokkan term operator di workflow kamu, lihat panduan [grouping](grouping#grouping-explanation).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.operators import MajoranaOperator, gamma\n"
"    >>> op = MajoranaOperator.from_dict({\n"
"    ...     (gamma(0, False),): 1.0,\n"
"    ...     (gamma(1, False),): 1.0,\n"
"    ...     (gamma(2, False), gamma(3, False)): 1.0\n"
"    ... })\n"
"    >>> # Assign group indices to terms\n"
"    >>> op.groups = [0, 0, 1]\n"
"    >>> # Partition operator by groups\n"
"    >>> grouped_ops = op.split_out_groups()\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    // Create operator with 3 terms\n"
"    QkComplex64 coeffs[3] = {{1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0}};\n"
"    uint32_t modes[4] = {0, 1, 2, 3};\n"
"    uint32_t boundaries[4] = {0, 1, 2, 4};\n"
"    QfMajoranaOperator *op = qf_maj_op_new(3, 4, coeffs, modes, boundaries);\n"
msgstr ""
"    // Create operator with 3 terms\n"
"    QkComplex64 coeffs[3] = {{1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0}};\n"
"    uint32_t modes[4] = {0, 1, 2, 3};\n"
"    uint32_t boundaries[4] = {0, 1, 2, 4};\n"
"    QfMajoranaOperator *op = qf_maj_op_new(3, 4, coeffs, modes, boundaries);\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    // Assign grouping information\n"
"    uint32_t groups[3] = {0, 0, 1};\n"
"    qf_maj_op_set_groups(op, groups, 3);\n"
msgstr ""
"    // Assign grouping information\n"
"    uint32_t groups[3] = {0, 0, 1};\n"
"    qf_maj_op_set_groups(op, groups, 3);\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    // Partition operator by groups\n"
"    QfMajoranaOperator *grouped_ops[2];\n"
"    qf_maj_op_split_out_groups(op, NULL, 0, grouped_ops);\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"    // Partition operator by groups\n"
"    QfMajoranaOperator *grouped_ops[2];\n"
"    qf_maj_op_split_out_groups(op, NULL, 0, grouped_ops);\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"id3\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Arithmetic and mathematical operations {#arithmetic-and-mathematical-operations}"
msgstr "Operasi aritmetika dan matematika {#arithmetic-and-mathematical-operations}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "All operators implement the [`OperatorTrait`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait\") protocol, which provides a unified set of operations across different operator types. This ensures that code written for one operator representation works uniformly with others. See [`qiskit_fermions.protocols`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/protocols#module-qiskit_fermions.protocols \"qiskit_fermions.protocols\") for how this protocol relates to the others this package defines.\n"
msgstr "Semua operator mengimplementasikan protokol [`OperatorTrait`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait\"), yang menyediakan kumpulan operasi terpadu untuk berbagai tipe operator. Jadi, kode yang ditulis untuk satu representasi operator juga bekerja sama persis dengan yang lain. Lihat [`qiskit_fermions.protocols`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/protocols#module-qiskit_fermions.protocols \"qiskit_fermions.protocols\") untuk mengetahui hubungan protokol ini dengan protokol lain yang didefinisikan paket ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The protocol includes arithmetic operations (such as addition, multiplication, and composition), structural operations (term iteration, mode support analysis, relabeling), mathematical functions (normal ordering, simplification, equivalence checking), and more. See the [`OperatorTrait`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait\") documentation for a complete reference of all available operations.\n"
msgstr "Protokol ini mencakup operasi aritmetika (seperti penjumlahan, perkalian, dan komposisi), operasi struktural (iterasi term, analisis dukungan mode, relabeling), fungsi matematika (normal ordering, penyederhanaan, pengecekan ekuivalensi), dan lainnya. Lihat dokumentasi [`OperatorTrait`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait\") untuk referensi lengkap semua operasi yang tersedia.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.operators import FermionOperator, cre, ann\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Construct a Hermitian operator: H = +0 -1 + +1 -0\n"
"    >>> op = FermionOperator.from_dict({\n"
"    ...     (cre(0), ann(1)): 1.0,\n"
"    ...     (cre(1), ann(0)): 1.0\n"
"    ... })\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Check if the operator is Hermitian\n"
"    >>> print(f\"Operator is Hermitian: {op.is_hermitian(atol=1e-10)}\")\n"
"    Operator is Hermitian: True\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    // Construct a Hermitian operator: H = +0 -1 + +1 -0\n"
"    QkComplex64 coeffs[2] = {{1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0}};\n"
"    bool actions[4] = {true, false, true, false};\n"
"    uint32_t modes[4] = {0, 1, 1, 0};\n"
"    uint32_t boundaries[3] = {0, 2, 4};\n"
"    QfFermionOperator *op = qf_ferm_op_new(2, 4, coeffs, actions, modes, boundaries);\n"
msgstr ""
"    // Construct a Hermitian operator: H = +0 -1 + +1 -0\n"
"    QkComplex64 coeffs[2] = {{1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0}};\n"
"    bool actions[4] = {true, false, true, false};\n"
"    uint32_t modes[4] = {0, 1, 1, 0};\n"
"    uint32_t boundaries[3] = {0, 2, 4};\n"
"    QfFermionOperator *op = qf_ferm_op_new(2, 4, coeffs, actions, modes, boundaries);\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    // Check if the operator is Hermitian\n"
"    bool is_hermitian = qf_ferm_op_is_hermitian(op, 1e-10);\n"
"    printf(\"Operator is Hermitian: %s\\n\", is_hermitian ? \"true\" : \"false\");\n"
msgstr ""
"    // Check if the operator is Hermitian\n"
"    bool is_hermitian = qf_ferm_op_is_hermitian(op, 1e-10);\n"
"    printf(\"Operator is Hermitian: %s\\n\", is_hermitian ? \"true\" : \"false\");\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    // Clean up\n"
"    qf_ferm_op_free(op);\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"    // Clean up\n"
"    qf_ferm_op_free(op);\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\" title=\"Note\">\n"
msgstr "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\" title=\"Catatan\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  [`is_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian\") verifies that $H - H^\\dagger = 0$ by reducing that difference to a normal form and comparing it against [`zero()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.zero \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.zero\"). Spelled out in terms of the other protocol operations, it performs the following:\n"
msgstr "  [`is_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian\") memverifikasi bahwa $H - H^\\dagger = 0$ dengan mereduksi selisih itu ke bentuk normal lalu membandingkannya dengan [`zero()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.zero \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.zero\"). Kalau dijabarkan dengan operasi protokol lainnya, langkah yang dilakukan adalah sebagai berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  The strength of this check depends on the operator type, because it depends on how completely that type’s normal form contracts adjacent generators. A `True` result is always reliable, but for some types a `False` result is conservative: see [`is_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian\") for details.\n"
msgstr "  Seberapa kuat pengecekan ini bergantung pada tipe operatornya, karena itu tergantung seberapa lengkap bentuk normal tipe tersebut mengontraksi generator yang bersebelahan. Hasil `True` selalu bisa diandalkan, tapi untuk beberapa tipe, hasil `False` bersifat konservatif: lihat [`is_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian\") untuk detailnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "</DoqAdmonition>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Important\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  The example uses `atol=1e-10`. The `atol` (absolute tolerance) parameter specifies a threshold. Coefficients with magnitude smaller than `atol` are treated as zero and discarded. This is essential for numerical stability when comparing operators, since floating-point arithmetic can introduce small rounding errors that would otherwise prevent equivalent operators from being recognized as such.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Penting\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  Contoh ini memakai `atol=1e-10`. Parameter `atol` (toleransi absolut) menentukan sebuah ambang batas. Koefisien dengan magnitudo lebih kecil dari `atol` dianggap nol dan dibuang. Ini penting buat stabilitas numerik saat membandingkan operator, karena aritmetika floating-point bisa menimbulkan galat pembulatan kecil yang kalau tidak ditangani akan membuat operator yang ekuivalen tidak dikenali sebagai ekuivalen.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Hint\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  While the [`OperatorTrait`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait\") protocol provides a common interface, individual operator implementations might offer additional convenience methods not part of the protocol. For example, [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\") and [`MajoranaOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-majorana-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.MajoranaOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.MajoranaOperator\") provide a `max_rank()` method that reports the length of their longest term. Always consult the API documentation for your operator type to discover all available functionality.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Petunjuk\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Meskipun protokol [`OperatorTrait`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait\") menyediakan antarmuka umum, implementasi operator tertentu mungkin menawarkan metode praktis tambahan yang bukan bagian dari protokol. Misalnya, [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\") dan [`MajoranaOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-majorana-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.MajoranaOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.MajoranaOperator\") menyediakan metode `max_rank()` yang melaporkan panjang term terpanjang mereka. Selalu cek dokumentasi API untuk tipe operator kamu supaya tahu semua fungsionalitas yang tersedia.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"operator-term-ordering\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Operator term ordering and normal forms {#operator-term-ordering-and-normal-forms}"
msgstr "Pengurutan term operator dan bentuk normal {#operator-term-ordering-and-normal-forms}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A fundamental challenge in quantum operator algebra is that mathematically equivalent operators can be represented in many different ways, each with different implications for quantum algorithms. The same operator can be written in algebraically equivalent forms (for example, $a^\\dagger b$ can be expressed as $ba^\\dagger + [a^\\dagger,b]$), yet these representations lead to different behavior in circuit synthesis, simplification, and numerical algorithms.\n"
msgstr "Tantangan mendasar dalam aljabar operator kuantum adalah operator yang secara matematis ekuivalen bisa direpresentasikan dalam banyak cara berbeda, masing-masing dengan implikasi berbeda untuk algoritma kuantum. Operator yang sama bisa ditulis dalam bentuk yang ekuivalen secara aljabar (misalnya, $a^\\dagger b$ bisa dinyatakan sebagai $ba^\\dagger + [a^\\dagger,b]$), tapi representasi-representasi ini menghasilkan perilaku yang berbeda dalam sintesis circuit, penyederhanaan, dan algoritma numerik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The operator representations support **normal ordering** operations that transform operators into algebra-specific canonical forms using commutation relations. This enables reliable comparisons (two equivalent operators have identical normal-ordered forms), reveals simplifications (commutation relations cause terms to cancel or combine), and supports algorithms that require specific operator forms for correctness and efficiency.\n"
msgstr "Representasi operator mendukung operasi **normal ordering** yang mengubah operator ke bentuk kanonik khusus aljabar dengan memakai relasi komutasi. Ini memungkinkan perbandingan yang andal (dua operator ekuivalen punya bentuk ternormal-urutkan yang identik), mengungkap penyederhanaan (relasi komutasi membuat term saling meniadakan atau bergabung), dan mendukung algoritma yang membutuhkan bentuk operator tertentu demi kebenaran dan efisiensi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Important\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  Different operator representations might implement normal ordering based on different commutation relations appropriate to their algebra. For example, fermionic normal ordering uses anticommutation relations ($\\{c_i, c_j^\\dagger\\} = \\delta_{ij}$), while Majorana normal ordering uses different algebra conventions ($\\{\\gamma_i, \\gamma_j\\} = 2\\delta_{ij}$). Always consult the documentation for your operator type to understand how normal ordering is implemented.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Penting\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  Representasi operator yang berbeda mungkin mengimplementasikan normal ordering berdasarkan relasi komutasi berbeda yang sesuai dengan aljabarnya. Misalnya, normal ordering fermionik memakai relasi antikomutasi ($\\{c_i, c_j^\\dagger\\} = \\delta_{ij}$), sedangkan normal ordering Majorana memakai konvensi aljabar yang berbeda ($\\{\\gamma_i, \\gamma_j\\} = 2\\delta_{ij}$). Selalu cek dokumentasi untuk tipe operator kamu supaya paham bagaimana normal ordering diimplementasikan.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.operators import FermionOperator, cre, ann\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Two different representations of the same operator\n"
"    >>> op1 = FermionOperator.from_dict({(ann(0), cre(0)): 1.0})\n"
"    >>> op2 = FermionOperator.from_dict({(): 1.0, (cre(0), ann(0)): -1.0})\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Direct comparison fails due to different forms\n"
"    >>> op1.equiv(op2, atol=1e-10)\n"
"    False\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Normal-order both and compare again\n"
"    >>> op1_normal = op1.normal_ordered()\n"
"    >>> op2_normal = op2.normal_ordered()\n"
"    >>> op1_normal.equiv(op2_normal, atol=1e-10)\n"
"    True\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```c\n"
"    #include <qiskit_fermions.h>\n"
"    #include <stdbool.h>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    // Two different representations of the same operator\n"
"    QkComplex64 coeff1[1] = {{1.0, 0.0}};\n"
"    bool actions1[2] = {false, true};\n"
"    uint32_t modes1[2] = {0, 0};\n"
"    uint32_t boundaries1[2] = {0, 2};\n"
"    QfFermionOperator *op1 = qf_ferm_op_new(1, 2, coeff1, actions1, modes1, boundaries1);\n"
msgstr ""
"    // Two different representations of the same operator\n"
"    QkComplex64 coeff1[1] = {{1.0, 0.0}};\n"
"    bool actions1[2] = {false, true};\n"
"    uint32_t modes1[2] = {0, 0};\n"
"    uint32_t boundaries1[2] = {0, 2};\n"
"    QfFermionOperator *op1 = qf_ferm_op_new(1, 2, coeff1, actions1, modes1, boundaries1);\n"

